      "message": "let\u0027s rephrase. maybe \"secdata_kernel: old version or doesn\u0027t exist\". and also set\nctx-\u003esecdata_error_code \u003d EC_ERROR_VBOOT_DATA_UNDERSIZED if read_tpm_nvmem() returns tpm_read_too_small.\n\n1) read_tpm_nvmem [as it is implemented now] can only return 2 error codes - tpm_read_not_found (if nvmem space doesn\u0027t exist) or tpm_read_too_small (if the requested size is bigger than the actual nvmem space).\n2) tpm_read_not_found is normal on the first boot: when we have already called load_ec_hash_() from ec_efs_init_(), but AP hasn\u0027t run yet and hasn\u0027t created the space yet.\n\nso, in fact, it\u0027s not a read_error. either there\u0027s no space or it is of the old format (smaller size). in both cases we already print something from inside read_tpm_nvmem(), but I wouldn\u0027t rely on that and still print something here.",
